  "note": "First election of the new Borough Council under the 1939 Municipal Charter: three councillors for each of the five wards, polled on Monday 15 May 1939. Nominations equalled seats in Curran, Gardenmore and Inver, whose members were returned unopposed; Central and Townparks were contested. Aldermen were to be appointed by the council at its first meeting. Three nominees for three seats. Dixon printed 'the Right Hon. Sir Thomas Dixon, Bart., H.M.L.' in the nomination report. Returned unopposed."
